  1: # Scholar-Flow Project Template
  2: 
  3: This project template provides a complete foundation for the Scholar-Flow AI-powered research paper collaboration platform as described in the [comprehensive README](README.md).
  4: 
  5: ## Project Structure
  6: 
  7: ```
  8: ├── apps/
  9: │   ├── frontend/          # Next.js frontend application
 10: │   └── backend/           # Node.js/Express backend API
 11: ├── docs/                  # Documentation
 12: └── scripts/               # Build and deployment scripts
 13: ```
 14: 
 15: ## Quick Start
 16: 
 17: ### Prerequisites
 18: 
 19: - Node.js 22+
 20: - PostgreSQL 15+ with pgvector extension
 21: - Redis (for background jobs)
 22: 
 23: ### Development Setup
 24: 
 25: 1. **Clone and install dependencies:**
 26: 
 27:    ```bash
 28:    # For Windows users, run the setup script
 29:       setup.bat
 30: 
 31:       # Or manually:
 32:       yarn install
 33:    ```
 34: 
 35: 2. **Set up environment variables:**
 36: 
 37:    ```bash
 38:    # Backend
 39:    cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
 40:    # Frontend
 41:    cp apps/frontend/.env.example apps/frontend/.env.local
 42:    ```
 43: 
 44: 3. **Configure database:**
 45: 
 46:    ```bash
 47:    # Update DATABASE_URL in both .env files
 48:    # Run migrations
 49:    yarn db:migrate
 50:    ```
 51: 
 52: 4. **Start development servers:**
 53:    ```bash
 54:    yarn dev
 55:    ```
 56: 
 57: This will start:
 58: 
 59: - Frontend: http://localhost:3000
 60: - Backend API: http://localhost:5000
 61: 
 62: ## Features Implemented
 63: 
 64: ### ✅ Basic Structure
 65: 
 66: - [x] Monorepo setup with Turbo
 67: - [x] Next.js frontend with TypeScript
 68: - [x] Express backend with TypeScript following Apollo Healthcare pattern
 69: - [x] Prisma schema with complete data model
 70: - [x] Backend modular architecture (modules/User, modules/Auth, etc.)
 71: - [x] Windows setup script (setup.bat)
 72: - [x] Environment configuration files
 73: - [x] GitHub Copilot instructions
 74: 
 75: ### 🚧 In Progress (Phase 1)
 76: 
 77: - [x] Complete User authentication module
 78: - [x] Frontend Auth.js setup
 79: - [ ] Paper upload and management
 80: - [x] Database migrations
 81: - [x] Frontend-backend integration
 82: 
 83: ### ⏳ Planned (Phase 1)
 84: 
 85: - [ ] File upload with cloud storage
 86: - [ ] Vector search with pgvector
 87: - [ ] AI features (OpenAI integration)
 88: - [ ] Basic collections functionality
 89: - [ ] User profile management
 90: 
 91: ## API Endpoints
 92: 
 93: The backend provides the following API endpoints:
 94: 
 95: - `GET /health` - Health check
 96: - `POST /api/auth/session/validate` - Validate JWT session
 97: - `GET /api/papers` - List papers
 98: - `GET /api/papers/:id` - Get paper details
 99: - Additional endpoints for annotations, collections, workspaces, etc.
100: 
101: ## Environment Variables
102: 
103: ### Backend (.env)
104: 
105: ```
106: DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...
107: NEXTAUTH_SECRET=your-secret-key
108: PORT=5000
109: FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
110: # Additional keys for AWS, OpenAI, Stripe, etc.
111: ```
112: 
113: ### Frontend (.env.local)
114: 
115: ```
116: NEXTAUTH_SECRET=your-secret-key
117: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
118: DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...
119: # OAuth provider keys
120: ```
121: 
122: ## Database Setup
123: 
124: 1. Install PostgreSQL with pgvector extension
125: 2. Create database: `scholar_flow`
126: 3. Run migrations: `yarn db:migrate`
127: 4. Generate Prisma client: `yarn db:generate`
128: 
129: ## Deployment
130: 
131: ### Frontend (Vercel)
132: 
133: - Deploy to Vercel with environment variables
134: - Set build command: `yarn build`
135: - Set output directory: `apps/frontend/.next`
136: 
137: ### Backend (Railway/Render/Fly.io)
138: 
139: - Deploy as Docker container or Node.js app
140: - Set start command: `yarn start`
141: - Configure environment variables
