  1: # Figma-Make to Production Migration Plan
  2: 
  3: Author: Copilot + Atik  
  4: Date: 2026-03-19  
  5: Status: In Progress
  6: 
  7: ## Objective
  8: 
  9: Migrate figma-make UI designs into production for public pages and auth pages while preserving existing app behavior and backend contracts.
 10: 
 11: Initial target pages:
 12: 
 13: - Home
 14: - Products (all subpages)
 15: - Resources (all subpages)
 16: - Company (all subpages)
 17: - Enterprise (all subpages)
 18: - Pricing
 19: - FAQ
 20: - Register
 21: - Login
 22: - Shared Navbar and Footer
 23: 
 24: ## Non-Negotiables
 25: 
 26: - Keep existing provider chain in app layout unchanged.
 27: - Keep existing auth endpoint contracts unless intentionally revised.
 28: - Preserve working billing checkout flow.
 29: - Avoid route regressions: all links must point to existing routes.
 30: - Use ToastProvider helpers, not direct Sonner imports.
 31: - Use Prisma Client model methods by default.
 32: - Use raw SQL only for complex or performance-critical cases.
 33: 
 34: ## Architecture Strategy
 35: 
 36: ### Frontend Strategy
 37: 
 38: 1. Shared layout first:
 39: 
 40: - Navbar
 41: - Footer
 42: - Route/link harmonization
 43: 
 44: 1. Section-by-section route migration:
 45: 
 46: - Products
 47: - Resources
 48: - Company
 49: - Enterprise
 50: - Home/Pricing/FAQ
 51: 
 52: 1. Auth migration:
 53: 
 54: - Register (UI + behavior-safe refactor)
 55: - Login (UI + behavior-safe refactor)
 56: - Keep callbackUrl and OAuth redirects compatible
 57: 
 58: 1. Reliability pass:
 59: 
 60: - Remove invalid links
 61: - Remove direct toast imports
 62: - Ensure responsive behavior
 63: - Ensure no hydration and TypeScript errors
 64: 
 65: ### Backend Strategy
 66: 
 67: 1. Contract freeze for Phase 1 migration:
 68: 
 69: - `/auth/register`
 70: - `/auth/signin`
 71: - `/auth/oauth/*`
 72: - `/billing/checkout-session`
 73: 
 74: 1. Backend changes only if required by frontend behavior:
 75: 
 76: - Keep response shape stable
 77: - Keep existing status code and error format conventions
 78: - Add validation if new fields are introduced
 79: 
 80: 1. Data access conventions:
 81: 
 82: - Default to Prisma Client methods for CRUD and relations
 83: - Use `$queryRaw`/`$executeRaw` only when Prisma cannot express needed SQL cleanly
 84: - Never use `$queryRawUnsafe`
 85: 
 86: ## Work Breakdown
 87: 
 88: ### Wave 1: Foundation (Current)
 89: 
 90: - [x] Footer migrated and route-safe links applied
 91: - [x] Register page moved to ToastProvider helpers
