<file path="docs/SETUP.md">
  1: # ScholarFlow Project - Setup Guide
  2: 
  3: ## 🏗️ Architecture Overview
  4: 
  5: ### Monorepo Structure
  6: 
  7: ```
  8: Project-Info/
  9: ├── apps/
 10: │   ├── frontend/          # Next.js 15 + React 19 + TypeScript
 11: │   └── backend/           # Node.js + Express + Prisma + PostgreSQL
 12: ├── packages/
 13: │   └── shared/            # Shared utilities (ready for expansion)
 14: ├── docs/                  # Documentation
 15: └── scripts/               # Setup and deployment scripts
 16: ```
 17: 
 18: ### Technology Stack
 19: 
 20: **Frontend (Next.js App)**
 21: 
 22: - ⚡ Next.js 15 with App Router
 23: - 🎨 Tailwind CSS + ShadCN UI components
 24: - 🔐 NextAuth.js for authentication
 25: - 🏪 Redux Toolkit Query for state management
 26: - 📱 Fully responsive design
 27: - 🎯 TypeScript for type safety
 28: 
 29: **Backend (Node.js API)**
 30: 
 31: - 🚀 Express.js with TypeScript
 32: - 🗄️ Prisma ORM with PostgreSQL
 33: - 🔒 JWT authentication with role-based access
 34: - 📊 Complete data models for papers, annotations, collections
 35: - 🎛️ API routes for all core features
 36: - 🛡️ Security middleware (CORS, Helmet, Rate Limiting)
 37: 
 38: ## 🚀 Quick Start
 39: 
 40: ### Prerequisites
 41: 
 42: - Node.js 20+ (LTS recommended)
 43: - Yarn 4.5+ (Berry)
 44: - PostgreSQL 15+ with pgvector extension
 45: - Redis (optional, for background jobs)
 46: 
 47: ### 1. Install Dependencies
 48: 
 49: ```bash
 50: yarn install
 51: ```
 52: 
 53: ### 2. Environment Setup
 54: 
 55: ```bash
 56: # Backend configuration
 57: cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
 58: 
 59: # Frontend configuration
 60: cp apps/frontend/.env.example apps/frontend/.env.local
 61: ```
 62: 
 63: For a complete list of variables and how to obtain them (Google/GitHub OAuth, S3, Stripe, etc.), see: [docs/ENVIRONMENT.md](docs/ENVIRONMENT.md)
 64: 
 65: ### 3. Configure Environment Variables
 66: 
 67: #### Backend (.env)
 68: 
 69: ```env
 70: DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/scholar_flow"
 71: NEXTAUTH_SECRET="your-secret-key-change-in-production"
 72: PORT=5000
 73: FRONTEND_URL="http://localhost:3000"
 74: NODE_ENV=development
 75: ```
 76: 
 77: #### Frontend (.env.local)
 78: 
 79: ```env
 80: NEXTAUTH_SECRET="your-secret-key-change-in-production"
 81: NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
 82: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL="http://localhost:5000/api"
 83: DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/scholar_flow"
 84: ```
 85: 
 86: ### 4. Database Setup
 87: 
 88: ```bash
 89: # Generate Prisma client
 90: yarn db:generate
 91: 
 92: # Run database migrations
 93: yarn db:migrate
 94: 
 95: # Seed sample data (optional)
 96: yarn db:seed
 97: ```
 98: 
 99: ### 5. Start Development Servers
100: 
101: ```bash
102: yarn dev
103: ```
104: 
105: This starts:
106: 
107: - **Frontend**: <http://localhost:3000> (per apps/frontend/package.json)
108: - **Backend API**: <http://localhost:5000>
109: 
110: Optional (Turborepo):
111: 
112: ```bash
113: yarn dev:turbo
114: ```
115: 
116: Note: Ensure ports 3000 and 5000 are free before running the Turbo dev task.
117: 
118: ## 📋 Available Scripts
119: 
120: ```bash
121: # Development
122: yarn dev                 # Start both frontend and backend
123: yarn build               # Build both applications
124: yarn type-check          # TypeScript type checking
125: yarn lint                # Lint both applications
126: 
127: # Database
128: yarn db:migrate          # Run Prisma migrations
129: yarn db:generate         # Generate Prisma client
130: yarn db:studio           # Open Prisma Studio
131: yarn db:seed             # Seed sample data
132: 
133: # Individual apps
134: cd apps/frontend && yarn dev    # Frontend only
135: cd apps/backend && yarn dev     # Backend only
136: ```
137: 
138: ## 🎯 What's Included
139: 
140: ### ✅ Completed Features
141: 
142: - **🏗️ Complete Project Structure**: Monorepo with frontend and backend
143: - **🔐 Authentication System**: NextAuth.js setup with JWT sessions
144: - **📊 Database Schema**: Complete Prisma schema with all models
145: - **🎨 UI Components**: Basic UI components with Tailwind CSS
146: - **📡 API Structure**: Express routes with proper middleware
147: - **🛡️ Security**: CORS, Helmet, Rate limiting, JWT validation
148: - **📱 Responsive Design**: Mobile-first responsive layout
149: - **⚡ Build System**: Turbo for optimized builds
150: - **📝 TypeScript**: Full TypeScript configuration
151: 
152: ### 🚧 Ready for Implementation
153: 
154: - **📄 File Upload**: S3 pre-signed URLs structure ready
155: - **🤖 AI Features**: OpenAI integration placeholder
156: - **🔍 Vector Search**: pgvector schema ready for embeddings
157: - **💳 Payments**: Stripe/SSLCommerz webhook structure
158: - **👥 Collaboration**: Real-time annotations structure
159: - **📊 Analytics**: Usage tracking models in place
160: 
161: ## 🔧 Development Workflow
162: 
163: ### 1. Frontend Development
164: 
165: ```bash
166: cd apps/frontend
167: yarn dev
168: ```
169: 
170: - Modify pages in `src/app/`
171: - Add components in `src/components/`
172: - Update API calls in `src/store/api/`
173: 
174: ### 2. Backend Development
175: 
176: ```bash
177: cd apps/backend
178: yarn dev
179: ```
180: 
181: - Add routes in `src/routes/`
182: - Modify middleware in `src/middleware/`
183: - Update database schema in `prisma/schema.prisma`
184: 
185: ### 3. Database Changes
186: 
187: ```bash
188: # After modifying schema.prisma
189: yarn db:migrate
190: yarn db:generate
191: ```
192: 
193: ## 🚀 Deployment
194: 
195: ### Frontend and Backend (Vercel Monorepo)
196: 
197: We deploy both apps on Vercel using the Monorepo + Turborepo flow. See: <https://vercel.com/docs/monorepos/turborepo>
198: 
199: Create two Vercel Projects pointing to different root directories in this repo:
200: 
201: 1. Frontend Project
202: 
203: - Root Directory: `apps/frontend`
204: - Framework Preset: Next.js
205: - Install Command: `yarn install`
206: - Build Command: `yarn build`
207: - Output: auto (Next.js)
208: - Env vars: copy from `apps/frontend/.env.example` to Vercel Project settings
209: 
210: 1. Backend Project (Express/Node)
211: 
212: - Root Directory: `apps/backend`
213: - Runtime: Node.js
214: - Install Command: `yarn install`
215: - Build Command: `yarn build` (runs `tsc` per package.json)
216: - Start Command (Preview/Dev only): `node dist/server.js`
217: - Env vars: copy from `apps/backend/.env.example` to Vercel Project settings
218: 
219: Important notes for the backend on Vercel:
220: 
221: - Vercel is serverless-first. Long-running servers (`app.listen`) are not supported on the Edge or Serverless Functions.
222: - For production on Vercel, expose your API via Serverless Functions. The common pattern is to export the Express `app` as the default handler from an `api/index.ts` and remove direct `app.listen` calls in that path.
223: - Until refactoring is complete, you can use Preview deployments for quick checks or deploy the backend to another host. We’ll add a serverless entrypoint in a follow-up.
224: 
225: Optional serverless entry (to be implemented later):
226: 
227: ```ts
228: // apps/backend/api/index.ts
229: import app from "../src/serverless-app"; // express app without app.listen
230: export default app;
231: ```
232: 
233: Then in `apps/backend/vercel.json` (optional):
234: 
235: ```json
236: {
237:   "functions": {
238:     "api/**/*.ts": { "runtime": "nodejs22.x" }
239:   },
240:   "routes": [{ "src": "/(.*)", "dest": "/api/index.ts" }]
241: }
242: ```
243: 
244: ## 🧪 Testing
245: 
246: The project is ready for testing:
247: 
248: - ✅ TypeScript compilation passes
249: - ✅ Build process completes successfully
250: - ✅ Development servers start correctly
251: - ✅ All dependencies installed properly
