<file path="README.md">
  1: # ScholarFlow
  2: 
  3: > **AI-Powered Research Paper Collaboration Hub**
  4: 
  5: ScholarFlow is a modern research paper management and collaboration platform designed to streamline academic workflows. Upload, organize, search, and collaborate on research papers with AI-powered insights and smart organization features.
  6: 
  7: [![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-1.1.9-blue)](./docs/Release.md)
  8: [![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache%202.0-green)](./LICENSE.md)
  9: [![TypeScript](https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-100%25-blue)](https://www.typescriptlang.org/)
 10: [![Next.js](https://img.shields.io/badge/Next.js-15-black)](https://nextjs.org/)
 11: [![Express](https://img.shields.io/badge/Express-Node.js-green)](https://expressjs.com/)
 12: 
 13: ## 🚀 Live Demo
 14: 
 15: - **Frontend**: [ScholarFlow App](https://scholar-flow-ai.vercel.app)
 16: - **API**: [Backend API](https://scholar-flow-api.vercel.app/api/health)
 17: 
 18: ## ✨ Features
 19: 
 20: ### � Rich Text Editing & Paper Management
 21: 
 22: - **Rich Text Editor**: Full-featured TipTap-based editor for research papers with advanced formatting, tables, lists, and more
 23: - **Auto-save & Drafts**: Debounced auto-save, manual save, and draft/publish workflow with real-time status
 24: - **Export to PDF/DOCX**: One-click export with embedded images and professional styling
 25: - **Image Upload**: Drag-and-drop or paste images directly into the editor, with S3 storage and resizing
 26: - **Smart Upload**: Drag-and-drop PDF upload with automatic metadata extraction
 27: - **AI Metadata**: Automatic title, author, and abstract extraction from PDFs
 28: - **Advanced Search**: Full-text search with filters (author, date, type, keywords)
 29: - **PDF Preview**: Secure in-app PDF viewer with responsive design
 30: 
 31: ### � Sharing & Collaboration
 32: 
 33: - **Email Sharing**: Share papers via email with permission management (view/edit)
 34: - **Workspace Collaboration**: Invite users to collections and workspaces with role-based access
 35: 
 36: - **Multiple Auth Options**: Google OAuth, GitHub OAuth, and email/password
 37: - **Secure Sessions**: JWT-based authentication with refresh tokens
 38: - **Password Recovery**: Secure password reset with email verification
 39: - **Production Security**: Rate limiting, input sanitization, CORS protection
 40: 
 41: ### 🎯 Modern UI/UX
 42: 
 43: - **Responsive Design**: Mobile-first design with Tailwind CSS
 44: - **Interactive Dashboard**: Quick access to papers, search, and collections
 45: - **Real-time Feedback**: Loading states, error handling, and success notifications
 46: - **Accessibility**: WCAG compliant with keyboard navigation support
 47: 
 48: ### � Billing & Subscription
 49: 
 50: - **Stripe Checkout**: Upgrade workspaces through secure hosted checkout with plan-aware metadata
 51: - **Customer Portal Access**: Manage billing details, cancel, or reactivate subscriptions from Stripe without support tickets
 52: - **Real-Time Sync**: Webhook-driven role updates keep dashboard permissions aligned with subscription status
 53: - **Billing Dashboard Entry**: Dedicated navigation item and refreshed auth session to surface plan changes instantly
 54: 
 55: ### �🔧 Admin Dashboard & System Monitoring
 56: 
 57: - **Real-Time System Metrics**: Live monitoring with 10-second auto-refresh for CPU, memory, storage, and database
 58: - **Accurate CPU Tracking**: Intelligent CPU usage calculation using idle/total times from Node.js os module
 59: - **Smart Storage Analytics**: Dynamic storage estimation based on actual database usage with realistic percentages
 60: - **Health Status Dashboard**: Comprehensive health cards (Database/Server/Storage/CPU) with automatic status classification
 61: - **Performance Visualization**: Auto-colored progress bars that adapt based on metric values (green→blue→yellow→red)
 62: - **System Information Panel**: Real-time platform, Node.js version, database version, memory, and uptime display
 63: - **Production-Grade Architecture**: HTTP caching, rate limiting, admin-only access, lazy loading with code splitting
 64: 
 65: ### 🏗️ Production-Ready Infrastructure
 66: 
 67: - **Performance Monitoring**: Response time tracking and health checks
 68: - **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error boundaries and retry logic
 69: - **Database Optimization**: Composite indexes and query optimization
 70: - **Scalable Architecture**: Microservices-ready with clean separation
 71: 
 72: ## 🛠️ Technology Stack
 73: 
 74: ### Frontend
 75: 
 76: - **Framework**: Next.js 15 with App Router
 77: - **Language**: TypeScript
 78: - **Styling**: Tailwind CSS + ShadCN UI
 79: - **State Management**: Redux Toolkit Query
 80: - **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod validation
 81: - **Authentication**: NextAuth.js
 82: 
 83: ### Backend
 84: 
 85: - **Runtime**: Node.js with Express.js
 86: - **Language**: TypeScript
 87: - **Database**: PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM
 88: - **Storage**: AWS S3 for file management
 89: - **Authentication**: JWT + bcrypt
 90: - **Validation**: Zod schemas
 91: 
 92: ### DevOps & Tools
 93: 
 94: - **Package Manager**: Yarn Berry (v4)
 95: - **Monorepo**: Turborepo for build optimization
 96: - **Database**: PostgreSQL with pgvector (AI-ready)
 97: - **Deployment**: Vercel (Frontend) + Railway/Render (Backend)
 98: - **Monitoring**: Health checks and performance tracking
 99: 
100: ## 📁 Project Structure
101: 
102: ```text
103: Scholar-Flow/
104: ├── apps/
105: │   ├── frontend/          # Next.js 15 application
106: │   │   ├── src/app/       # App Router pages
107: │   │   ├── components/    # Reusable UI components
108: │   │   ├── lib/          # Utilities and configurations
109: │   │   └── redux/        # State management
110: │   └── backend/          # Express.js API server
111: │       ├── src/app/      # Application logic
112: │       ├── prisma/       # Database schema and migrations
113: │       └── scripts/      # Utility scripts
114: ├── docs/                 # Project documentation
115: ├── .github/             # GitHub workflows and templates
116: └── .cursor/             # Development rules and guidelines
117: ```
118: 
119: ## 🚀 Quick Start
120: 
121: ### Prerequisites
122: 
123: - Node.js 18+
124: - PostgreSQL 15+
125: - Yarn Berry (v4)
126: - AWS S3 account (for file storage)
127: 
128: ### Installation
129: 
130: 1. **Clone the repository**
131: 
132:    ```bash
133:    git clone https://github.com/Atik203/Scholar-Flow.git
134:    cd Scholar-Flow
135:    ```
136: 
137: 2. **Install dependencies**
138: 
139:    ```bash
140:    yarn install
141:    ```
142: 
143: 3. **Set up environment variables**
144: 
145:    ```bash
146:    # Copy environment templates
147:    cp apps/frontend/.env.example apps/frontend/.env.local
148:    cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
149: 
150:    # Edit the .env files with your configurations
151:    ```
152: 
153: 4. **Set up the database**
154: 
155:    ```bash
156:    yarn db:migrate
157:    yarn db:generate
158:    ```
159: 
160: 5. **Start development servers**
161: 
162:    ```bash
163:    yarn dev:turbo
164:    ```
165: 
166:    The application will be available at:
167:    - Frontend: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
168:    - Backend: [http://localhost:5000](http://localhost:5000)
169: 
170: ## 🔧 Development Commands
171: 
172: ```bash
173: # Development
174: yarn dev:turbo          # Start both frontend and backend
175: yarn dev:frontend       # Start only frontend
176: yarn dev:backend        # Start only backend
177: 
178: # Database
179: yarn db:migrate         # Run database migrations
180: yarn db:generate        # Generate Prisma client
181: yarn db:studio          # Open Prisma Studio
182: yarn db:seed            # Seed database with sample data
183: 
184: # Quality Assurance
185: yarn lint               # Run ESLint
186: yarn type-check         # TypeScript compilation check
187: yarn test               # Run test suite
188: yarn build              # Production build
189: 
190: # Utilities
191: yarn clean              # Clean build artifacts
192: yarn reset              # Reset node_modules and rebuild
193: ```
194: 
195: ### Content Management & Editing
196: 
197: - ✅ **Rich Text Editor**: TipTap-based, with advanced formatting, tables, lists, and image upload
198: - ✅ **Auto-save & Drafts**: Debounced auto-save, manual save, and draft/publish workflow
199: - ✅ **Export to PDF/DOCX**: One-click export with embedded images and professional styling
200: - ✅ **Image Upload**: Drag-and-drop or paste images, S3 storage, resizing
201: - ✅ **Email Sharing**: Share papers via email with permission management
202: 
203: ### Authentication & Security
204: 
205: - ✅ **Authentication System**: Google/GitHub OAuth + email/password
206: - ✅ **Production Security**: Rate limiting, monitoring, error handling, admin-only access
207: 
208: ### Paper Management
