286: ## Additional Constraints from .cursor/rules/ (read-only source)
287: 
288: ### Backend Module Architecture
289: - Feature modules live under `apps/backend/src/app/modules/` with structure: controller, service, routes, validation schemas.
290: - Routes register ONLY in `apps/backend/src/app/routes` — never register ad-hoc routes elsewhere.
291: - Controllers must be thin; all business logic belongs in services.
292: - Services use Prisma client from shared singleton; handle transactions explicitly when needed.
293: - Zod for request body, param, and query validation; reject early on failure.
294: 
295: ### Database Operations — $queryRaw Critical Rule
296: - CRITICAL: All database operations MUST use `$queryRaw` or `$executeRaw` instead of standard Prisma Client methods for optimal performance.
297: - This applies to: SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, aggregation, complex joins.
298: - Use template literal syntax for SQL injection prevention: `WHERE email = ${email}`
299: - Use `prisma.$queryRaw<Type[]>` for proper typing.
300: - Select only required fields; never use `SELECT *`.
301: - Use `LIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${skip}` for pagination; never return unbounded lists.
302: - EXCEPTION — OAuth operations MUST keep standard Prisma Client upsert:
303:   - `createAccount()`
304:   - `createOrUpdateUser()`
305:   - `createOrUpdateUserWithOAuth()`
306:   Changing these to raw queries causes P2002 unique constraint errors.
307: 
308: ### TypedSQL & Raw SQL Files
309: - Raw SQL statements live in `apps/backend/prisma/sql/` with ONE statement per file.
310: - File names must be valid JavaScript identifiers (no leading dashes) because they become generated function names.
311: - Use positional parameters `$1`, `$2` with optional `-- @param {Type} $1:name` comments.
312: - After adding/modifying SQL, run `yarn db:generate` to regenerate typed functions.
313: - Import generated functions from `@prisma/client/sql`.
314: - Execute typed queries with `prisma.$queryRawTyped(queryName(...params))` or `prisma.$queryRaw(...)`.
315: - Always apply pending migrations BEFORE running `prisma generate --sql`.
316: - Every new TypedSQL query must have at least one test verifying shape and performance assumptions.
317: - Above any raw query usage, add a comment referencing the originating `.sql` file.
318: 
319: ### Frontend Component & Design Standards
320: - Prefer Next.js Server Components; add `"use client"` ONLY when interactivity or state is required.
321: - Use `next/image` and `next/font`; stream large UI with Suspense to avoid unnecessary client bundles.
322: - Consult `docs/UI_DESIGN.md` BEFORE creating new pages or components.
323: - Component taxonomy:
324:   - `components/auth/` — Authentication related
325:   - `components/layout/` — Navigation, headers, sidebars
326:   - `components/ui/` — ShadCN primitives
327:   - `components/customUI/` — Custom components
328: - Design system: OKLCH color system, `max-w-[1440px]` container width, established Typography heading scales.
329: - Use existing hover effects (lift, scale, glow) and transitions.
330: - SEO: use Metadata API; ensure canonical URLs; plan sitemap + robots when routes stabilize.
331: - Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance, proper ARIA labels, roles, focus states, keyboard navigation.
332: 
333: ### Sonner Toast & Error Handling Patterns
334: - Use Sonner via ToastProvider functions ONLY:
335:   - `showErrorToast`, `showSuccessToast` from `@/components/providers/ToastProvider`
336:   - `showApiErrorToast` from `@/lib/errorHandling`
337: - NEVER import `toast` directly from `sonner`.
338: - Use custom error handling hooks:
339:   - `useErrorHandler` for generic errors
340:   - `useQueryErrorHandler` for RTK Query queries
341:   - `useMutationErrorHandler` for mutations
342: - Smart retry: auto-retry on network/server errors, manual retry for client errors.
343: - Error classification: Network (retry), Client 4xx (fix required), Server 5xx (retry).
344: - All auth methods must use try/catch with `ApiError` for consistent error responses.
345: - Feature-specific error classes must extend `ApiError` with standardized format:
346:   ```typescript
347:   {
348:     success: false,
349:     message: string,
350:     statusCode: number,
351:     errorCode?: string,
352:     details?: object,
353:     timestamp: string
354:   }
355:   ```
356: 
357: ### Production-Ready Security & Performance Standards
358: - Debug logging is allowed ONLY in development; always gate with `process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production"`.
359: - Replace all `any` types with proper interfaces (e.g., `AuthenticatedRequest`).
360: - Apply feature-specific rate limiters to all mutation endpoints, especially uploads.
361: - Use `performanceMonitor` middleware and add `X-Response-Time` headers.
362: - Health check endpoints must exist:
363:   - `/api/health` — Basic health status
364:   - `/api/health/detailed` — Full system health
365:   - `/api/health/live` — Kubernetes liveness probe
366:   - `/api/health/ready` — Kubernetes readiness probe
367: - BigInt handling: cast to integer in SQL for JSON serialization to avoid issues.
368: - Memory monitoring: track heap usage and memory thresholds in health checks.
369: 
370: ### pgvector Detailed Rules
371: - Only run similarity queries if `USE_PGVECTOR=true`.
372: - `PaperChunk.embedding` column type is `vector`; migrations manage any transition from JSON fallback.
373: - Use a service helper to format float arrays into vector literals (`[x,y,z]`).
374: - Similarity operators: `<->` (L2), `<=>` (cosine), `<#>` (negative inner product). Align index operator class with chosen operator.
375: - Create IVF index (`ivfflat`) only after sufficient data volume; document chosen `lists` parameter.
376: - Limit result sets (e.g., `LIMIT 10`); avoid full vector scans.
377: - Guard against mismatched dimensionality; validate embedding array length before insert.
378: - Add round-trip test (insert + similarity query) when modifying embedding logic.
379: 
380: ### Auth Specifics
381: - Frontend authentication state is managed via Redux Toolkit (in addition to NextAuth session).
382: - OAuth account creation MUST use standard Prisma upsert pattern; do NOT convert to raw SQL.
383: - Password strength indicators on register forms.
384: - Auth guards for protected routes.
385: - All auth functions must have JSDoc comments.
386: - Authentication-related code requires minimum 90% test coverage.
387: - Comprehensive integration tests required for all auth endpoints and flows.
388: 
389: ### Workflow & Documentation Discipline
390: - Follow phase discipline strictly; see `Roadmap.md` before starting new features.
391: - Ship only in-phase work; defer out-of-scope requests unless they unblock the current milestone.
392: - Prefer shipping a thin vertical slice over broad incomplete scaffolding.
393: - Do NOT create README.md, OPTIMIZATION.md, CHANGELOG.md, or PERFORMANCE.md files for minor updates or every change.
394: - Inline documentation only; comments explain WHY not WHAT.
395: - Quality gates before merge:
396:   1. `yarn build` succeeds
397:   2. `yarn type-check` clean
398:   3. `yarn lint` zero errors
399:   4. Tests pass; add/adjust tests for new logic
400:   5. No secrets committed
401:   6. No obvious N+1 or unbounded queries
402:   7. WCAG 2.1 AA for new UI components
403:   8. Migrations are additive (backwards compatible)
404:   9. Update public docs (README, SCHEMA, ENVIRONMENT) for changed public behavior
405:   10. Keep PR scope tight with summary + checklist
406: 
407: ### Development Server Ports
408: - Frontend dev server: port 3000
409: - Backend dev server: port 5000
