<file path="docs/Chapter4-System-Design-Diagrams.md">
   1: # Chapter 4 — System Design (Diagram Drawing Spec)
   2: 
   3: This document is a **diagram-drawing blueprint** for ScholarFlow. It is written so you can recreate the system design diagrams in **Figma / Lucidchart / Draw.io** by copying the **exact node labels** and **arrow labels**.
   4: 
   5: Scope (MVP + adjacent modules already present in codebase): **Auth**, **User Profile**, **Workspaces**, **Collections**, **Papers + Editor**, **AI Summary/Insights**, **Citations**, **Discussions**, **Activity Log**, **Billing (Stripe)**.
   6: 
   7: ---
   8: 
   9: ## 0) Notation + Naming (use everywhere)
  10: 
  11: ### 0.1 Shape legend (recommended)
  12: 
  13: - **External Actor**: stick figure
  14: - **External System**: rectangle
  15: - **ScholarFlow (System Boundary)**: big container box
  16: - **Internal Component**: rectangle with component name
  17: - **DFD Process**: rounded rectangle (P1, P2, …)
  18: - **DFD Data Store**: open-ended rectangle (D1, D2, …)
  19: - **Data Flow**: arrow with a _noun phrase_ label
  20: 
  21: ### 0.2 Environments / endpoints (labels)
  22: 
  23: - **Frontend (Next.js)**: “ScholarFlow Web App (Next.js)”
  24: - **Backend (Express)**: “ScholarFlow API (Express)”
  25: - **API base path**: `/api/*`
  26: - **Important route groups**:
  27:   - `/api/auth` (register/login/oauth, sessions, verify email, forgot/reset)
  28:   - `/api/user`
  29:   - `/api/workspaces`
  30:   - `/api/collections`
  31:   - `/api/papers`
  32:   - `/api/editor`
  33:   - `/api/citations`
  34:   - `/api/discussions`
  35:   - `/api/activity-log`
  36:   - `/api/billing`
  37:   - `/api/health`
  38: 
  39: ### 0.3 Core actors (use these names)
  40: 
  41: - **Guest User** (not signed in)
  42: - **Authenticated User** (signed in)
  43: - **Workspace Owner**
  44: - **Workspace Member**
  45: - **Collection Owner**
  46: - **Collection Member**
  47: - **Admin**
  48: 
  49: Role enum (backend): `RESEARCHER | PRO_RESEARCHER | TEAM_LEAD | ADMIN`
  50: 
  51: ---
  52: 
  53: ## 1) Context Diagram (System Context)
  54: 
  55: ### 1.1 Context diagram goal
  56: 
  57: Show ScholarFlow as a single system and all external parties/systems it communicates with.
  58: 
  59: ### 1.2 Nodes (copy/paste labels)
  60: 
  61: | Node ID | Label (exact)                                       | Type               | Notes                                |
  62: | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------ |
  63: | A1      | Guest User                                          | External Actor     | Browses, registers, logs in          |
  64: | A2      | Authenticated User                                  | External Actor     | Uploads papers, collaborates         |
  65: | A3      | Admin                                               | External Actor     | Admin endpoints, moderation, ops     |
  66: | E1      | OAuth Provider (Google)                             | External System    | OAuth sign-in                        |
  67: | E2      | OAuth Provider (GitHub)                             | External System    | OAuth sign-in                        |
  68: | E3      | Email Service (SMTP/Gmail)                          | External System    | Verification, reset, invites         |
  69: | E4      | Stripe                                              | External System    | Billing + webhooks                   |
  70: | E5      | AI Provider (OpenAI/Gemini/Deepseek)                | External System    | Summaries, insights                  |
  71: | E6      | AWS S3 (Object Storage)                             | External System    | Paper files, previews, editor images |
  72: | E7      | Document Conversion Service (Gotenberg/LibreOffice) | External System    | DOC/DOCX → PDF preview               |
  73: | E8      | Redis (Queue/Cache)                                 | External System    | Background processing queue          |
  74: | S1      | ScholarFlow Web App (Next.js)                       | Internal Component | UI, NextAuth client flows            |
  75: | S2      | ScholarFlow API (Express)                           | Internal Component | REST API under `/api/*`              |
  76: | S3      | PostgreSQL Database                                 | Internal Component | Prisma/Postgres core store           |
  77: 
  78: ### 1.3 Edges (copy/paste arrow labels)
  79: 
  80: | From | To  | Arrow label (exact)                          | Protocol/Notes         |
  81: | ---- | --- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
  82: | A1   | S1  | Browse public pages, start auth              | HTTPS                  |
  83: | A2   | S1  | Use dashboard, manage work                   | HTTPS                  |
  84: | S1   | S2  | API requests (JWT/session)                   | HTTPS JSON + multipart |
  85: | S2   | S3  | Read/write app data                          | SQL (Prisma)           |
  86: | S2   | E6  | Upload/download objects, presign URLs        | S3 API                 |
  87: | S2   | E3  | Send verification/reset/invite emails        | SMTP                   |
  88: | S2   | E1  | OAuth token exchange / profile fetch         | OAuth                  |
  89: | S2   | E2  | OAuth token exchange / profile fetch         | OAuth                  |
  90: | S2   | E4  | Create checkout/session, manage subscription | Stripe API             |
  91: | E4   | S2  | Stripe webhooks (billing events)             | `/webhooks/stripe`     |
  92: | S2   | E5  | Generate summary/insights                    | HTTPS                  |
  93: | S2   | E7  | Convert document to preview PDF              | HTTPS                  |
  94: | S2   | E8  | Enqueue/process background jobs              | Redis                  |
  95: 
  96: ### 1.4 Optional Context Diagram (Mermaid)
