 121: 
 122: ## 2) Use Case Diagram + Descriptive Forms
 123: 
 124: ### 2.1 Use case diagram: actors
 125: 
 126: ScholarFlow exposes a single role enum in the backend: `RESEARCHER | PRO_RESEARCHER | TEAM_LEAD | ADMIN`. The table below maps every actor used in the diagrams to that enum so role-based permissions stay consistent.
 127: 
 128: | Actor ID | Actor name                           | Role enum mapping                              | Notes / Responsibilities                                                                  |
 129: | -------- | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
 130: | ACT-01   | Guest User                           | —                                              | Not authenticated; can browse marketing pages, register, request password reset, verify.  |
 131: | ACT-02   | Researcher (default authenticated)   | `RESEARCHER`                                   | Baseline signed-in user; can join workspaces, upload/view papers within quota.            |
 132: | ACT-03   | Pro Researcher                       | `PRO_RESEARCHER`                               | Paid tier; inherits Researcher rights plus AI features and larger quotas.                 |
 133: | ACT-04   | Team Lead / Workspace Owner          | `TEAM_LEAD`                                    | Creates/owns workspaces, manages billing, invitations, approvals, and workspace settings. |
 134: | ACT-05   | Workspace Member                     | `RESEARCHER` or `PRO_RESEARCHER` (invited)     | Any authenticated user invited into a workspace; permissions derived from membership.     |
 135: | ACT-06   | Collection Owner / Collection Member | `RESEARCHER`, `PRO_RESEARCHER`, or `TEAM_LEAD` | Derived from workspace membership; permissions scoped by collection role (VIEW/EDIT).     |
 136: | ACT-07   | Admin                                | `ADMIN`                                        | Platform-level operator for moderation, compliance, billing overrides, feature flags.     |
 137: 
 138: ### 2.2 Use case diagram: use cases (core)
 139: 
 140: Use these IDs as your ellipse labels.
 141: 
 142: | UC ID | Use case name (exact)                     | Primary actor(s)             | Role scope                                                               | Related API groups                    |
 143: | ----- | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |
 144: | UC-01 | Register Account (Email/Password)         | Guest User                   | Guest (pre-auth) selects eventual Researcher/Pro/Team Lead role          | `/api/auth`                           |
 145: | UC-02 | Login (Email/Password)                    | Guest User                   | Guest (pre-auth)                                                         | `/api/auth`                           |
 146: | UC-03 | Login (OAuth: Google/GitHub)              | Guest User                   | Guest (pre-auth)                                                         | `/api/auth`                           |
 147: | UC-04 | Verify Email                              | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead, Admin (self-verification)         | `/api/auth`                           |
 148: | UC-05 | Request Password Reset                    | Guest User                   | Guest (pre-auth)                                                         | `/api/auth`                           |
 149: | UC-06 | Reset Password                            | Guest User                   | Guest (pre-auth)                                                         | `/api/auth`                           |
 150: | UC-07 | View/Update Profile                       | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead, Admin (profile owner)             | `/api/user`                           |
 151: | UC-08 | Create Workspace                          | Authenticated User           | Pro Researcher, Team Lead, Admin (acting on behalf)                      | `/api/workspaces`                     |
 152: | UC-09 | Invite Member to Workspace                | Workspace Owner              | Team Lead (owner) or Admin (override)                                    | `/api/workspaces` + Email             |
 153: | UC-10 | Accept/Decline Workspace Invitation       | Workspace Member             | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead (invitee)                          | `/api/workspaces`                     |
 154: | UC-11 | Create Collection                         | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead (workspace member)                 | `/api/collections`                    |
 155: | UC-12 | Invite Member to Collection               | Collection Owner             | Collection Owner (Researcher/Pro/Team Lead) or Admin override            | `/api/collections` + Email            |
 156: | UC-13 | Accept/Decline Collection Invitation      | Collection Member            | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead (invitee)                          | `/api/collections`                    |
 157: | UC-14 | Upload Paper (PDF/DOCX/DOC)               | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead, Admin (audit upload)              | `/api/papers` + S3                    |
 158: | UC-15 | View Paper (metadata + file access)       | Authenticated User           | Workspace members (Researcher/Pro/Team Lead) and Admin (read-only)       | `/api/papers` + S3                    |
 159: | UC-16 | Generate Preview (DOC/DOCX)               | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead                                    | `/api/papers` + Conversion + S3       |
 160: | UC-17 | Process Paper (extract + chunk)           | Authenticated User (trigger) | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead trigger; Admin can force reprocess | `/api/papers` + Redis + DB            |
 161: | UC-18 | Create Draft in Editor                    | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead                                    | `/api/editor`                         |
 162: | UC-19 | Update Draft Content                      | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead                                    | `/api/editor`                         |
 163: | UC-20 | Publish Draft                             | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead (with publish permission)          | `/api/editor`                         |
 164: | UC-21 | Generate AI Summary                       | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead (feature-flag dependent)           | `/api/papers` + AI Provider           |
 165: | UC-22 | Generate AI Insights (thread/messages)    | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead (feature-flag dependent)           | `/api/papers` + AI Provider           |
 166: | UC-23 | Add Paper to Collection                   | Collection Member (EDIT)     | Collection Member with EDIT permission (Researcher/Pro/Team Lead)        | `/api/collections`                    |
 167: | UC-24 | Remove Paper from Collection              | Collection Member (EDIT)     | Collection Member with EDIT permission (Researcher/Pro/Team Lead)        | `/api/collections`                    |
 168: | UC-25 | Export Citations                          | Authenticated User           | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead                                    | `/api/citations`                      |
 169: | UC-26 | Start Discussion Thread                   | Workspace/Collection Member  | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead                                    | `/api/discussions`                    |
 170: | UC-27 | Post Discussion Message                   | Workspace/Collection Member  | Researcher, Pro Researcher, Team Lead                                    | `/api/discussions`                    |
 171: | UC-28 | View Activity Log                         | Authenticated User           | Researcher (own events), Pro Researcher, Team Lead, Admin (all events)   | `/api/activity-log`                   |
 172: | UC-29 | Manage Subscription                       | Authenticated User           | Team Lead (workspace owner) and Admin (billing override)                 | `/api/billing` + Stripe               |
 173: | UC-30 | Admin Operations                          | Admin                        | Admin only                                                               | `/api/admin`                          |
 174: | UC-31 | Moderate Flagged Paper                    | Admin                        | Admin only                                                               | `/api/admin/papers`, `/api/papers`    |
 175: | UC-32 | Manage User Roles & Workspace Escalations | Admin                        | Admin only                                                               | `/api/admin/roles`, `/api/workspaces` |
 176: | UC-33 | Run System Health & Compliance Checks     | Admin                        | Admin only                                                               | `/api/admin`, `/api/health/*`         |
 177: 
 178: ### 2.3 Use case descriptive forms (copy/paste templates)
 179: 
 180: Below are the **recommended** descriptive forms for the most important flows. Use the same headings in your SRS/Chapter 4.
 181: 
 182: #### UC-01 — Register Account (Email/Password)
 183: 
 184: - **Primary Actor**: Guest User
 185: - **Trigger**: User submits registration form
 186: - **Inputs (UI fields)**: `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`, `institution?`, `fieldOfStudy?`, `password`, `role?`
 187: - **Preconditions**: User is not authenticated
 188: - **Postconditions (Success)**: `User` created; session/JWT issued; verification email may be sent
 189: - **Main Flow**:
 190:   1. User enters details and submits.
 191:   2. Web App calls API to create user.
 192:   3. API validates and stores user.
 193:   4. API responds with auth/session payload.
 194: - **Alternative/Exception Flows**:
 195:   - Email already used → return validation error.
 196:   - Weak password → return validation error.
 197: - **Related API**: `/api/auth` (register)
 198: - **Primary Data Stores**: `User`
 199: 
 200: #### UC-02 — Login (Email/Password)
 201: 
 202: - **Primary Actor**: Guest User
 203: - **Trigger**: User submits login form
 204: - **Inputs (UI fields)**: `email`, `password`, `rememberMe?`
 205: - **Preconditions**: Account exists and is not deleted
 206: - **Postconditions (Success)**: Session/JWT issued; user is authenticated in Web App
 207: - **Main Flow**:
 208:   1. User enters email/password.
 209:   2. Web App calls API.
 210:   3. API validates credentials.
 211:   4. API returns auth/session payload.
 212: - **Alternative/Exception Flows**:
 213:   - Invalid credentials → return auth error.
 214: - **Related API**: `/api/auth` (login/signin)
 215: - **Primary Data Stores**: `User`, `Session`
 216: 
 217: #### UC-03 — Login (OAuth: Google/GitHub)
 218: 
 219: - **Primary Actor**: Guest User
 220: - **Trigger**: User clicks “Continue with Google/GitHub”
 221: - **Inputs**: OAuth authorization code (provider callback)
 222: - **Preconditions**: Provider account accessible
 223: - **Postconditions (Success)**: `Account` linked; `User` created/updated; session established
 224: - **Main Flow**:
 225:   1. Web App redirects user to OAuth provider.
 226:   2. Provider returns authorization code.
 227:   3. API exchanges code for tokens.
 228:   4. API fetches profile and upserts `User`/`Account`.
 229:   5. API issues session/JWT.
 230: - **Related Systems**: OAuth Provider (Google/GitHub)
 231: - **Related API**: `/api/auth` (oauth)
 232: - **Primary Data Stores**: `User`, `Account`, `Session`
