 658: 
 659: ## 4) Activity Diagrams (core workflows)
 660: 
 661: Activity diagrams below are written in **lane-friendly steps** so you can convert them to a swimlane diagram in Figma/Lucid.
 662: 
 663: ### 4.1 Activity — Paper Upload (PDF/DOCX/DOC)
 664: 
 665: **Swimlanes**: User | Web App | API | S3 | DB
 666: 
 667: 1. User selects file and clicks Upload.
 668: 2. Web App validates file type/size client-side.
 669: 3. Web App sends multipart request to API.
 670: 4. API authenticates request.
 671: 5. API validates fields: `workspaceId?`, `title?`, `authors?`, `year?`, `source?`.
 672: 6. API uploads file to S3 (`objectKey`).
 673: 7. API inserts `Paper` row.
 674: 8. API inserts `PaperFile` row linked to paper.
 675: 9. API returns upload success + `paperId` + `processingStatus=UPLOADED`.
 676: 
 677: (Optional) Trigger processing: 10. Web App calls “Process paper”. 11. API enqueues extraction job.
 678: 
 679: Mermaid validator:
 680: 
 681: ```mermaid
 682: sequenceDiagram
 683:   participant U as User
 684:   participant W as Web App
 685:   participant A as API
 686:   participant S as AWS S3
 687:   participant D as Postgres DB
 688: 
 689:   U->>W: Select file + Upload
 690:   W->>A: POST /api/papers (multipart)
 691:   A->>A: Auth + validate fields
 692:   A->>S: PutObject(file)
 693:   A->>D: Insert Paper + PaperFile
 694:   D-->>A: ok
 695:   A-->>W: {paperId, processingStatus: UPLOADED}
 696:   W-->>U: Show uploaded paper
 697: ```
 698: 
 699: ### 4.2 Activity — Accept Workspace Invitation
 700: 
 701: **Swimlanes**: User | Email | Web App | API | DB
 702: 
 703: 1. Workspace Owner triggers invite (separate UC).
 704: 2. Email service sends invite email with link.
 705: 3. User opens link (may require login).
 706: 4. Web App calls API: “accept invitation”.
 707: 5. API validates invitation status is `PENDING`.
 708: 6. API creates/ensures `WorkspaceMember` record.
 709: 7. API updates `WorkspaceInvitation.status = ACCEPTED` and sets `acceptedAt`.
 710: 8. Web App shows workspace available.
 711: 
 712: ```mermaid
 713: sequenceDiagram
 714:   participant U as User
 715:   participant E as Email Service
 716:   participant W as Web App
 717:   participant A as API
 718:   participant D as Postgres DB
 719: 
 720:   E->>U: Send invite email
 721:   U->>W: Open invite link
 722:   W->>A: POST /api/invitations/accept
 723:   A->>D: Validate PENDING status
 724:   A->>D: Create WorkspaceMember
 725:   A->>D: Update Invitation (ACCEPTED)
 726:   A-->>W: Success
 727:   W-->>U: Show workspace
 728: ```
 729: 
 730: ### 4.3 Activity — Reset Password
 731: 
 732: **Swimlanes**: User | Web App | API | Email | DB
 733: 
 734: 1. User opens “Forgot password”.
 735: 2. Web App submits `email`.
 736: 3. API creates reset token and stores it.
 737: 4. API sends reset email.
 738: 5. User clicks reset link.
 739: 6. Web App submits `token` + `newPassword`.
 740: 7. API validates token and updates password hash.
 741: 8. API invalidates token.
 742: 9. Web App shows success.
 743: 
 744: ```mermaid
 745: sequenceDiagram
 746:   participant U as User
 747:   participant W as Web App
 748:   participant A as API
 749:   participant E as Email Service
 750:   participant D as Postgres DB
 751: 
 752:   U->>W: Request "Forgot Password"
 753:   W->>A: POST /api/auth/forgot
 754:   A->>D: Store reset token
 755:   A->>E: Send reset email
 756:   E-->>U: Reset link
 757:   U->>W: Click link + Enter new password
 758:   W->>A: POST /api/auth/reset
 759:   A->>D: Validate token + hash password
 760:   A->>D: Invalidate token
 761:   A-->>W: Success
 762:   W-->>U: Login page
 763: ```
 764: 
 765: ### 4.4 Activity — Generate AI Summary
 766: 
 767: **Swimlanes**: User | Web App | API | DB | AI Provider
 768: 
 769: 1. User clicks “Generate summary” on a paper.
 770: 2. Web App requests summary generation.
 771: 3. API authorizes request and loads paper + chunks.
 772: 4. API builds prompt and calls AI provider.
 773: 5. AI provider returns summary.
 774: 6. API stores summary in `AISummary`.
 775: 7. API returns summary to Web App.
 776: 
 777: ```mermaid
 778: sequenceDiagram
 779:   participant U as User
 780:   participant W as Web App
 781:   participant A as API
 782:   participant D as Postgres DB
 783:   participant AI as AI Provider
 784: 
 785:   U->>W: Click "Generate Summary"
 786:   W->>A: POST /api/papers/{id}/summary
 787:   A->>D: Fetch paper + chunks
 788:   A->>AI: Send prompt
 789:   AI-->>A: Return summary
 790:   A->>D: Insert AISummary
 791:   A-->>W: Return summary text
 792:   W-->>U: Display summary
 793: ```
 794: 
 795: ### 4.5 Activity — Publish Draft (Editor)
 796: 
 797: **Swimlanes**: User | Web App | API | DB
 798: 
 799: 1. User opens a draft paper in the editor.
 800: 2. User clicks “Publish”.
 801: 3. Web App submits publish request (`title?`, `abstract?`).
 802: 4. API authorizes request and validates draft state.
 803: 5. API updates paper fields: `isDraft=false`, `isPublished=true` (and metadata/title/abstract if provided).
 804: 6. API records activity log event (if enabled).
 805: 7. Web App refreshes and displays the published paper.
 806: 
 807: ```mermaid
 808: sequenceDiagram
 809:   participant U as User
 810:   participant W as Web App
 811:   participant A as API
 812:   participant D as Postgres DB
 813: 
 814:   U->>W: Editor -> Publish
 815:   W->>A: POST /api/editor/publish
 816:   A->>A: Auth + validate draft
 817:   A->>D: Update Paper (isPublished=true)
 818:   A->>D: Log Activity
 819:   A-->>W: Success
 820:   W-->>U: Show published paper
 821: ```
